{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39471916",
      "title": "Imperative Animations",
      "sourceHash": "4a0345abce5d86cc6fb0529dff0e4d1a5ffe2921a164716472463e5bb9bc26af",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "So at this point you already know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 6.09,
          "en": "a lot about using Framer Motion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.09,
          "end": 10.32,
          "en": "with those motion components to animate things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 13.02,
          "en": "And up to this point in this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.02,
          "end": 16.26,
          "en": "we used the default approach of working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.26,
          "end": 20.34,
          "en": "with Framer Motion by using these motion components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.34,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "and by defining all the animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 26.13,
          "en": "and all the animation settings declaratively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.13,
          "end": 29.13,
          "en": "in our JSX code through props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 32.43,
          "en": "That's the default and that's how you will define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.43,
          "end": 36.303,
          "en": "and control most of your animations with Framer Motion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 40.17,
          "en": "But sometimes you encounter scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 44.37,
          "en": "or use cases where you maybe wanna start an animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 47.97,
          "en": "imperatively instead of declaratively.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.97,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "And therefore I'll also show you how that could be done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 54.75,
          "en": "And for that, let's assume that if the user submits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 56.58,
          "en": "an invalid form here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.58,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "so if the input fields are empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 62.58,
          "en": "or at least one input field is empty, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 66.27,
          "en": "that we wanna shake all these input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.27,
          "end": 68.7,
          "en": "That could be a little animation we might wanna play",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.7,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "if a user tries to submit this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 74.703,
          "en": "without entering valid values in those input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "And whilst we could definitely also achieve this goal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "in a declarative way, here I'll show you how you could do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 84.99,
          "en": "in a imperative way because Framer Motion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.99,
          "end": 87.9,
          "en": "also supports this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.9,
          "end": 91.26,
          "en": "For that, we first of all have to import a hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.26,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "from Framer Motion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 95.733,
          "en": "We have to import the useAnimate hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.56,
          "end": 100.83,
          "en": "This hook can then be called in our component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 101.85300000000001,
          "en": "like all hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.05,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "And this hook then returns an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "that contains two important elements:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 113.283,
          "en": "a scope element, and an animate element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 117.50999999999999,
          "en": "The names of course are up to you, but the first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.50999999999999,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "will be a ref, which you can add to elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 125.01,
          "en": "and I'll explain why and where to add it soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.01,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "And the second element, animate, will be a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "you can use in your code to imperatively trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 133.923,
          "en": "a certain animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "Now let's start with that function here actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "And for that, let's go to the place where the animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 144.87,
          "en": "should be triggered, which is inside of this if statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "Here, I'm checking if any of the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 149.37,
          "en": "contains an invalid value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 152.073,
          "en": "and if that's the case at the moment, I just return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.84,
          "en": "Now I instead want to call animate here to trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.84,
          "end": 161.84,
          "en": "some animation and shake those input and textarea elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.91,
          "end": 165.24,
          "en": "To achieve this, you can pass a string to animate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.24,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "where you use a CSS selector to target the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 171.81,
          "en": "that should be animated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.81,
          "end": 175.563,
          "en": "For example, all input and textarea elements like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.49,
          "end": 180.42,
          "en": "You could also look for CSS classes if you had them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.42,
          "end": 184.023,
          "en": "But here I'll just use the input and textarea tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.31,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "As a second argument to animate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 189,
          "en": "you can then pass an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189,
          "end": 192.75,
          "en": "where you describe the animation that should be played.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.75,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "And that's the same kind of object you would pass to exit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "or initial or animate or to your variance down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "So it's an object like this where you define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 207.633,
          "en": "which properties should be animated to which values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.71,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "So for example here, we could animate the exposition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 216.07,
          "en": "to move the elements along the X axis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "and then define some key frames here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 224.013,
          "en": "so that maybe we first move them to the left by 10 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.18,
          "end": 228.96,
          "en": "then back to the middle, then to the right by 10 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 228.96,
          "end": 231.06,
          "en": "and then back to the middle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 234.78,
          "en": "so that we shake every element from left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.78,
          "end": 236.49,
          "en": "And of course you could animate more,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.49,
          "end": 238.59,
          "en": "the opacity, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 241.26,
          "en": "But here for me it's just the X position",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.26,
          "end": 242.41,
          "en": "that I want to animate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.16,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "As a third argument you can then also pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 250.11,
          "en": "a configuration object to animate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.11,
          "end": 251.58,
          "en": "that allows you to configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.58,
          "end": 253.563,
          "en": "how the animation will be played.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.67,
          "end": 258.72,
          "en": "That would be the equivalent to this transition prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.72,
          "end": 262.653,
          "en": "or this transition property, you can add to your variance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 267.87,
          "en": "So in there, in this last object, you can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 271.86,
          "en": "make sure that it's a spring animation that's being played.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 271.86,
          "end": 273.78,
          "en": "You can control the duration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.78,
          "end": 276.693,
          "en": "for example, set this to 0.2 seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.77,
          "end": 280.38,
          "en": "And you can also do something fancy here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "you can add a delay property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "which allows you to set a delay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 287.223,
          "en": "after which the animation will start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.42,
          "end": 291.42,
          "en": "Now that on its own is not that fancy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.42,
          "end": 293.7,
          "en": "even though it sometimes can be helpful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 293.7,
          "end": 296.58,
          "en": "but it gets fancy if we combine it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.58,
          "end": 299.43,
          "en": "with another imperative function we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.43,
          "end": 303.06,
          "en": "from Framer Motion because from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.06,
          "end": 305.943,
          "en": "we can also import a stagger function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 307.02,
          "end": 309.66,
          "en": "And stagger might sound familiar to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.66,
          "end": 312.84,
          "en": "we used the staggerChildren setting before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.84,
          "end": 315.72,
          "en": "to make sure that the animations on the child items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 315.72,
          "end": 319.86,
          "en": "of this list get staggered so that delays are inserted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.86,
          "end": 323.493,
          "en": "between the different animations of the different items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.42,
          "end": 327.63,
          "en": "And this stagger function simply allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 327.63,
          "end": 329.16,
          "en": "to do the same thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 329.16,
          "end": 331.8,
          "en": "if we're setting up an imperative animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.8,
          "end": 333.903,
          "en": "so if we're using the animate function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.83,
          "end": 338.1,
          "en": "Because then we can set delay here to stagger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 338.1,
          "end": 341.733,
          "en": "and then our stagger amount like 0.05.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.04,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "And this will then achieve the same as staggerChildren",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 350.79,
          "en": "did before here on this unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.79,
          "end": 353.85,
          "en": "It will add delays between the different animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 356.46,
          "en": "for the different elements that are targeted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 356.46,
          "end": 361.32,
          "en": "by this selector, so that we don't shake them simultaneously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 361.32,
          "end": 362.733,
          "en": "but after each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 363.72,
          "end": 367.02,
          "en": "And that's how we can trigger an animation imperatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 367.02,
          "end": 369.57,
          "en": "from inside our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 369.57,
          "end": 372.363,
          "en": "But that alone won't do the trick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 377.88,
          "en": "You might recall that here we also had this scope element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 377.88,
          "end": 380.78,
          "en": "in that array that was returned by useAnimate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 381.952,
          "end": 386.73,
          "en": "And this scope thing here is in the end a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 386.73,
          "end": 390.03,
          "en": "as we could create it ourselves with useRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 390.03,
          "end": 393.42,
          "en": "that should be connected to a JSX element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 393.42,
          "end": 396.96,
          "en": "that's scopes the selector we're setting up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 396.96,
          "end": 398.433,
          "en": "in the animate function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 399.78,
          "end": 403.59000000000003,
          "en": "So that we're not selecting input and textarea elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 403.59000000000003,
          "end": 407.493,
          "en": "from all over the page, but from a selected area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 409.05,
          "end": 411.12,
          "en": "For that, we should add the ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 411.12,
          "end": 414.24,
          "en": "to this form and pass this scope ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 414.24,
          "end": 417.243,
          "en": "as a value for this ref prop to this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 419.15999999999997,
          "end": 422.19,
          "en": "And now animate will only select inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 422.19,
          "end": 424.17,
          "en": "and text areas inside of this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 424.17,
          "end": 426.303,
          "en": "and not anywhere else on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 427.56,
          "end": 430.11,
          "en": "And with that, we're using useAnimate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 430.11,
          "end": 432.72,
          "en": "to trigger our animation imperatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 432.72,
          "end": 435.18,
          "en": "and therefore here, if I click Add Challenge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 435.18,
          "end": 439.95,
          "en": "with invalid inputs, you see that those inputs are shaking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 439.95,
          "end": 442.62,
          "en": "and they're not shaking simultaneously,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 442.62,
          "end": 445.983,
          "en": "but instead in this staggered manner after each other.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}